quran[16]{c,v,t}:
  15,16,"Indeed, We have set up constellations (of stars) in the sky (in the form of galaxies) and adorned them for the onlookers."
  15,17,"And We have protected them from every outcast Satan (i.e. every destructive force),"
  15,18,"except for the one who steals a hearing, then a discernible flame (such as a shooting star or meteor) follows him."
  15,19,"As for the earth, We have spread it out and set firm mountains in it. And We caused to grow in it every well-balanced thing."
  15,20,And We have placed in it (various) means of livelihood for you and all those (creatures) to whom you do not provide sustenance.
  15,21,"And there is not a thing (on this earth), but its means of sustenance are with Us, and We do not send it down except in a precise measure."
  15,22,"And We send the fertilising winds, then send down water from the clouds, so that We provide it for you to drink. And you are not the keepers of its resources."
  15,23,"Indeed, it is We Who give life and cause death, and We are the Inheritors (i.e. the Owners of everything)."
  15,24,"And We indeed know those of you who were predecessors, and We indeed know the successors."
  15,25,"Indeed, your Lord is the One Who will gather them (on the Day of Resurrection). Indeed, He is All-Wise, All-Knowing."
  15,26,"Indeed, We created human being from sounding dried clay, moulded from ageing, dark mud."
  15,27,"As for the jinn, We created them earlier from scorching smokeless fire."
  15,28,"And (remember) when your Lord said to the angels: ‘Indeed I am going to create a human from sounding dried clay, moulded from ageing, dark mud."
  15,29,"So when I have proportioned him and breathed My Spirit into him, then fall down in prostration before him.’"
  15,30,"So the angels prostrated, all of them together,"
  15,31,but Iblis (did not). He refused to be with those who prostrated.
